---@field nullable? boolean Optional. Indicates if the value may be null.
---@field title? string Optional. The title of the schema.
---@field ref? string Optional. Allows indirect references between schema nodes. The value should be a valid reference to a child of the root `defs`. For example, the following schema defines a reference to a schema node named "Pet": ``` type: object properties: pet: ref: #/defs/Pet defs: Pet: type: object properties: name: type: string ``` The value of the "pet" property is a reference to the schema node named "Pet". See details in https://json-schema.org/understanding-json-schema/structuring.
---@field required? gcp.ces_v1.StringList Optional. Required properties of Type.OBJECT.
---@field anyOf? gcp.ces_v1.Ces_SchemaList Optional. The value should be validated against any (one or more) of the subschemas in the list.
---@field type? gcp.ces_v1.Ces_SchemaTypeEnum|string Required. The type of the data.
---@field minimum? number Optional. Minimum value for Type.INTEGER and Type.NUMBER.
---@field uniqueItems? boolean Optional. Indicate the items in the array must be unique. Only applies to TYPE.ARRAY.
---@field minItems? string Optional. Minimum number of the elements for Type.ARRAY.
---@field items? gcp.ces_v1.Ces_Schema Optional. Schema of the elements of Type.ARRAY.

