---@field supervisor? gcp.ces_v1.GuardrailSupervisor Optional. Guardrail that runs supervisor intervention.
---@field description? string Optional. Description of the guardrail.
---@field llmPromptSecurity? gcp.ces_v1.GuardrailLlmPromptSecurity Optional. Guardrail that blocks the conversation if the prompt is considered unsafe based on the LLM classification.
---@field name? string Identifier. The unique identifier of the guardrail. Format: `projects/{project}/locations/{location}/apps/{app}/guardrails/{guardrail}`
---@field enabled? boolean Optional. Whether the guardrail is enabled.
---@field etag? string Etag used to ensure the object hasn't changed during a read-modify-write operation. If the etag is empty, the update will overwrite any concurrent changes.
---@field displayName? string Required. Display name of the guardrail.

---Guardrail that blocks the conversation based on the code callbacks provided.
---@class gcp.ces_v1.GuardrailCodeCallback
---@field beforeModelCallback? gcp.ces_v1.Callback Optional. The callback to execute before the model is called. If there are multiple calls to the model, the callback will be executed multiple times. Each callback function is expected to return a structure (e.g., a dict or object) containing at least: - 'decision': Either 'OK' or 'TRIGGER'. - 'reason': A string explaining the decision. A 'TRIGGER' decision may halt further processing.
---@field afterAgentCallback? gcp.ces_v1.Callback Optional. The callback to execute after the agent is called. Each callback function is expected to return a structure (e.g., a dict or object) containing at least: - 'decision': Either 'OK' or 'TRIGGER'. - 'reason': A string explaining the decision. A 'TRIGGER' decision may halt further processing.
---@field beforeAgentCallback? gcp.ces_v1.Callback Optional. The callback to execute before the agent is called. Each callback function is expected to return a structure (e.g., a dict or object) containing at least: - 'decision': Either 'OK' or 'TRIGGER'. - 'reason': A string explaining the decision. A 'TRIGGER' decision may halt further processing.
---@field afterModelCallback? gcp.ces_v1.Callback Optional. The callback to execute after the model is called. If there are multiple calls to the model, the callback will be executed multiple times. Each callback function is expected to return a structure (e.g., a dict or object) containing at least: - 'decision': Either 'OK' or 'TRIGGER'. - 'reason': A string explaining the decision. A 'TRIGGER' decision may halt further processing.

---Guardrail that bans certain content from being used in the conversation.
---@class gcp.ces_v1.GuardrailContentFilter
---@field sensitiveWordsExemptions? gcp.ces_v1.StringList Optional. Entries of the sensitive words list that this guardrail allows. Only valid when match_type is SENSITIVE_WORDS. Each value must equal a list entry (case-insensitive, surrounding whitespace ignored); other values have no effect. Applies to this guardrail only. At most 1000 entries of up to 256 characters each.
---@field disregardDiacritics? boolean Optional. If true, diacritics are ignored during matching.
---@field bannedContentsInAgentResponse? gcp.ces_v1.StringList Optional. List of banned phrases. Applies only to agent responses.
---@field bannedContents? gcp.ces_v1.StringList Optional. List of banned phrases. Applies to both user inputs and agent responses.
---@field bannedContentsInUserInput? gcp.ces_v1.StringList Optional. List of banned phrases. Applies only to user inputs.
---@field matchType? gcp.ces_v1.GuardrailContentFilterMatchTypeEnum|string Required. Match type for the content filter.

---@alias gcp.ces_v1.GuardrailContentFilterMatchTypeEnum "MATCH_TYPE_UNSPECIFIED"|"SIMPLE_STRING_MATCH"|"WORD_BOUNDARY_STRING_MATCH"|"REGEXP_MATCH"|"SENSITIVE_WORDS"

---@alias gcp.ces_v1.GuardrailList gcp.ces_v1.Guardrail[]

---Guardrail that blocks the conversation if the LLM response is considered violating the policy based on the LLM classification.
---@class gcp.ces_v1.GuardrailLlmPolicy
---@field modelSettings? gcp.ces_v1.ModelSettings Optional. Model settings.
---@field allowShortUtterance? boolean Optional. By default, the LLM policy check is bypassed for short utterances. Enabling this setting applies the policy check to all utterances, including those that would normally be skipped.
---@field prompt? string Required. Policy prompt. Supports session variable placeholders (`{var}`) as well as `{agent_system_instruction}` to inject the agent's resolved system instructions.
---@field failOpen? boolean Optional. If an error occurs during the policy check, fail open and do not trigger the guardrail.
---@field maxConversationMessages? number Optional. When checking this policy, consider the last 'n' messages in the conversation. When not set a default value of 10 will be used.
---@field policyScope? gcp.ces_v1.GuardrailLlmPolicyPolicyScopeEnum|string Required. Defines when to apply the policy check during the conversation. If set to `POLICY_SCOPE_UNSPECIFIED`, the policy will be applied to the user input. When applying the policy to the agent response, additional latency will be introduced before the agent can respond.

---@alias gcp.ces_v1.GuardrailLlmPolicyPolicyScopeEnum "POLICY_SCOPE_UNSPECIFIED"|"USER_QUERY"|"AGENT_RESPONSE"|"USER_QUERY_AND_AGENT_RESPONSE"

---Guardrail that blocks the conversation if the input is considered unsafe based on the LLM classification.
---@class gcp.ces_v1.GuardrailLlmPromptSecurity
---@field customPolicy? gcp.ces_v1.GuardrailLlmPolicy Optional. Use a user-defined LlmPolicy to configure the security guardrail.
---@field defaultSettings? gcp.ces_v1.GuardrailLlmPromptSecurityDefaultSecuritySettings Optional. Use the system's predefined default security settings. To select this mode, include an empty 'default_settings' message in the request. The 'default_prompt_template' field within will be populated by the server in the response.
---@field failOpen? boolean Optional. Determines the behavior when the guardrail encounters an LLM error. - If true: the guardrail is bypassed. - If false (default): the guardrail triggers/blocks. Note: If a custom policy is provided, this field is ignored in favor of the policy's 'fail_open' configuration.

---Configuration for default system security settings.
---@class gcp.ces_v1.GuardrailLlmPromptSecurityDefaultSecuritySettings
---@field defaultPromptTemplate? string Output only. The default prompt template used by the system. This field is for display purposes to show the user what prompt the system uses by default. It is OUTPUT_ONLY.

---Model safety settings overrides. When this is set, it will override the default settings and trigger the guardrail if the response is considered unsafe.
---@class gcp.ces_v1.GuardrailModelSafety
---@field safetySettings? gcp.ces_v1.GuardrailModelSafetySafetySettingList Required. List of safety settings.

---Safety setting.
---@class gcp.ces_v1.GuardrailModelSafetySafetySetting
---@field threshold? gcp.ces_v1.GuardrailModelSafetySafetySettingThresholdEnum|string Required. The harm block threshold.
---@field category? gcp.ces_v1.GuardrailModelSafetySafetySettingCategoryEnum|string Required. The harm category.

---@alias gcp.ces_v1.GuardrailModelSafetySafetySettingCategoryEnum "HARM_CATEGORY_UNSPECIFIED"|"HARM_CATEGORY_HATE_SPEECH"|"HARM_CATEGORY_DANGEROUS_CONTENT"|"HARM_CATEGORY_HARASSMENT"|"HARM_CATEGORY_SEXUALLY_EXPLICIT"|"HARM_CATEGORY_PROFANITY"|"HARM_CATEGORY_TOXIC"

---@alias gcp.ces_v1.GuardrailModelSafetySafetySettingList gcp.ces_v1.GuardrailModelSafetySafetySetting[]

---@alias gcp.ces_v1.GuardrailModelSafetySafetySettingThresholdEnum "HARM_BLOCK_THRESHOLD_UNSPECIFIED"|"BLOCK_LOW_AND_ABOVE"|"BLOCK_MEDIUM_AND_ABOVE"|"BLOCK_ONLY_HIGH"|"BLOCK_NONE"|"OFF"

---Guardrail that runs supervisor intervention.
---@class gcp.ces_v1.GuardrailSupervisor
---@field type? gcp.ces_v1.GuardrailSupervisorTypeEnum|string Optional. The type of the supervisor.
---@field detectionMode? gcp.ces_v1.GuardrailSupervisorDetectionModeEnum|string Optional. The detection mode of the supervisor.

---@alias gcp.ces_v1.GuardrailSupervisorDetectionModeEnum "DETECTION_MODE_UNSPECIFIED"|"NON_BLOCKING"|"BLOCKING"

---@alias gcp.ces_v1.GuardrailSupervisorTypeEnum "TYPE_UNSPECIFIED"|"INVALID_TEXT"|"LANGUAGE_SHIFT"|"SPEAKER_SHIFT"|"AUDIO_MISMATCH"|"MISSING_TOOL_CALL"|"CUSTOM"|"CHOPPY_AUDIO"|"PROFANITY"

---Represents an image input or output in the conversation.
---@class gcp.ces_v1.Image
---@field data? string Required. Raw bytes of the image.
---@field altText? string Optional. The alternative text for the image.
---@field mimeType? string Required. The IANA standard MIME type of the source data. Supported image types includes: * image/png * image/jpeg * image/webp

---@class gcp.ces_v1.ImportAppProjectsLocationsAppsRequest
---@field jsonPatchContent? string Optional. Patch content as a JSON string.
---@field importOptions? gcp.ces_v1.ImportAppRequestImportOptions Optional. Options governing the import process for the app.
---@field gcsUri? string The [Google Cloud Storage](https://cloud.google.com/storage/docs/) URI from which to import app. The format of this URI must be `gs:///`.
---@field appContent? string Raw bytes representing the compressed zip file with the app folder structure.
---@field ignoreAppLock? boolean Optional. Flag for overriding the app lock during import. If set to true, the import process will ignore the app lock.
---@field jsonPatchGcsUri? string Optional. A Cloud Storage URI pointing to a JSON file containing the patches.
---@field appId? string Optional. The ID to use for the imported app. * If not specified, a unique ID will be automatically assigned for the app. * Otherwise, the imported app will use this ID as the final component of its resource name. If an app with the same ID already exists at the specified location in the project, the content of the existing app will be replaced.
---@field displayName? string Optional. The display name of the app to import. * If the app is created on import, and the display name is specified, the imported app will use this display name. If a conflict is detected with an existing app, a timestamp will be appended to the display name to make it unique. * If the app is a reimport, this field should not be set. Providing a display name during reimport will result in an INVALID_ARGUMENT error.
---@field parent string Required. The parent resource name with the location of the app to import.

---Configuration options for the app import process. These options control how the import behaves, particularly when conflicts arise with existing app data.
---@class gcp.ces_v1.ImportAppRequestImportOptions
---@field validateOnly? boolean Optional. Flag for dry-running the import process. If set to true, the import process will only perform validations and will not make any changes to the existing app or create a new one.
---@field conflictResolutionStrategy? gcp.ces_v1.ImportAppRequestImportOptionsConflictResolutionStrategyEnum|string Optional. The strategy to use when resolving conflicts during import.

---@alias gcp.ces_v1.ImportAppRequestImportOptionsConflictResolutionStrategyEnum "CONFLICT_RESOLUTION_STRATEGY_UNSPECIFIED"|"REPLACE"|"OVERWRITE"

---InputAudioConfig configures how the CES agent should interpret the incoming audio data.
---@class gcp.ces_v1.InputAudioConfig
---@field sampleRateHertz? number Required. The sample rate (in Hertz) of the input audio data.
---@field noiseSuppressionLevel? string Optional. Whether to enable noise suppression on the input audio. Available values are "low", "moderate", "high", "very_high".
---@field audioEncoding? gcp.ces_v1.InputAudioConfigAudioEncodingEnum|string Required. The encoding of the input audio data.

---@alias gcp.ces_v1.InputAudioConfigAudioEncodingEnum "AUDIO_ENCODING_UNSPECIFIED"|"LINEAR16"|"MULAW"|"ALAW"

---Ephemeral Meta credentials for Instagram native integration.
---@class gcp.ces_v1.InstagramCredentials
---@field authCode? string Required. The Meta auth code provided by the embedded signup flow.
---@field conversationProfileId? string Optional. The Conversation Profile ID to use for the deployment.

---@alias gcp.ces_v1.IntegerList number[]

---Language settings of the app.
---@class gcp.ces_v1.LanguageSettings
---@field enableMultilingualSupport? boolean Optional. Enables multilingual support. If `true`, agents in the app will use pre-built instructions to improve handling of multilingual input.
---@field defaultLanguageCode? string Optional. The default language code of the app.
---@field fallbackAction? string Optional. Deprecated: This feature is no longer supported. Use `enable_multilingual_support` instead to improve handling of multilingual input. The action to perform when an agent receives input in an unsupported language. This can be a predefined action or a custom tool call. Valid values are: - A tool's full resource name, which triggers a specific tool execution. - A predefined system action, such as "escalate" or "exit", which triggers an EndSession signal with corresponding metadata to terminate the conversation.
---@field supportedLanguageCodes? gcp.ces_v1.StringList Optional. List of languages codes supported by the app, in addition to the `default_language_code`.

---Defines a security scheme using an API key.
---@class gcp.ces_v1.LfA2aV1APIKeySecurityScheme
---@field name? string Required. The name of the header, query, or cookie parameter to be used.
---@field location? string Required. The location of the API key. Valid values are "query", "header", or "cookie".
---@field description? string An optional description for the security scheme.

---Defines optional capabilities supported by an agent.
---@class gcp.ces_v1.LfA2aV1AgentCapabilities
---@field pushNotifications? boolean Indicates if the agent supports sending push notifications for asynchronous task updates.
---@field extensions? gcp.ces_v1.LfA2aV1AgentExtensionList A list of protocol extensions supported by the agent.
---@field streaming? boolean Indicates if the agent supports streaming responses.
---@field extendedAgentCard? boolean Indicates if the agent supports providing an extended agent card when authenticated.

---A self-describing manifest for an agent. It provides essential metadata including the agent's identity, capabilities, skills, supported communication methods, and security requirements. Next ID: 20
---@class gcp.ces_v1.LfA2aV1AgentCard
---@field name? string Required. A human readable name for the agent. Example: "Recipe Agent"
---@field capabilities? gcp.ces_v1.LfA2aV1AgentCapabilities Required. A2A Capability set supported by the agent.
---@field version? string Required. The version of the agent. Example: "1.0.0"
---@field provider? gcp.ces_v1.LfA2aV1AgentProvider The service provider of the agent.
---@field defaultInputModes? gcp.ces_v1.StringList Required. protolint:enable REPEATED_FIELD_NAMES_PLURALIZED The set of interaction modes that the agent supports across all skills. This can be overridden per skill. Defined as media types.
---@field iconUrl? string Optional. A URL to an icon for the agent.
---@field supportedInterfaces? gcp.ces_v1.LfA2aV1AgentInterfaceList Required. Ordered list of supported interfaces. The first entry is preferred.
---@field defaultOutputModes? gcp.ces_v1.StringList Required. The media types supported as outputs from this agent.
---@field description? string Required. A human-readable description of the agent, assisting users and other agents in understanding its purpose. Example: "Agent that helps users with recipes and cooking."
---@field signatures? gcp.ces_v1.LfA2aV1AgentCardSignatureList JSON Web Signatures computed for this `AgentCard`.
---@field securityRequirements? gcp.ces_v1.LfA2aV1SecurityRequirementList Security requirements for contacting the agent.
---@field securitySchemes? gcp.ces_v1.LfA2aV1SecuritySchemeMap The security scheme details used for authenticating with this agent.
---@field skills? gcp.ces_v1.LfA2aV1AgentSkillList Required. Skills represent the abilities of an agent. It is largely a descriptive concept but represents a more focused set of behaviors that the agent is likely to succeed at.
---@field documentationUrl? string A URL providing additional documentation about the agent.

---AgentCardSignature represents a JWS signature of an AgentCard. This follows the JSON format of an RFC 7515 JSON Web Signature (JWS).
---@class gcp.ces_v1.LfA2aV1AgentCardSignature
---@field protected? string Required. Required. The protected JWS header for the signature. This is always a base64url-encoded JSON object.
---@field signature? string Required. The computed signature, base64url-encoded.
---@field header? gcp.ces_v1.DocumentMap The unprotected JWS header values.

---@alias gcp.ces_v1.LfA2aV1AgentCardSignatureList gcp.ces_v1.LfA2aV1AgentCardSignature[]

---A declaration of a protocol extension supported by an Agent.
---@class gcp.ces_v1.LfA2aV1AgentExtension
---@field uri? string The unique URI identifying the extension.
---@field required? boolean If true, the client must understand and comply with the extension's requirements.
---@field params? gcp.ces_v1.DocumentMap Optional. Extension-specific configuration parameters.
---@field description? string A human-readable description of how this agent uses the extension.

---@alias gcp.ces_v1.LfA2aV1AgentExtensionList gcp.ces_v1.LfA2aV1AgentExtension[]

---Declares a combination of a target URL, transport and protocol version for interacting with the agent. This allows agents to expose the same functionality over multiple protocol binding mechanisms.
---@class gcp.ces_v1.LfA2aV1AgentInterface
---@field tenant? string Optional. An opaque string used for routing requests to a specific agent or tenant when multiple agents are served behind a single A2A endpoint. When set, clients MUST include this value in the `tenant` field of all request messages sent to this interface. The server is responsible for interpreting the value and routing requests accordingly; the protocol does not define its format or semantics.
---@field url? string Required. The URL where this interface is available. Must be a valid absolute HTTPS URL in production. Example: "https://api.example.com/a2a/v1", "https://grpc.example.com/a2a"
---@field protocolBinding? string Required. The protocol binding supported at this URL. This is an open form string, to be easily extended for other protocol bindings. The core ones officially supported are `JSONRPC`, `GRPC` and `HTTP+JSON`.
---@field protocolVersion? string Required. The version of the A2A protocol this interface exposes. Use the latest supported minor version per major version. Examples: "0.3", "1.0"

---@alias gcp.ces_v1.LfA2aV1AgentInterfaceList gcp.ces_v1.LfA2aV1AgentInterface[]

---Represents the service provider of an agent.
---@class gcp.ces_v1.LfA2aV1AgentProvider
---@field url? string Required. A URL for the agent provider's website or relevant documentation. Example: "https://ai.google.dev"
---@field organization? string Required. The name of the agent provider's organization. Example: "Google"

---Represents a distinct capability or function that an agent can perform.
