---@field refreshUrl? string The URL to be used for obtaining refresh tokens.

---Defines configuration details for the OAuth 2.0 Device Code flow (RFC 8628). This flow is designed for input-constrained devices such as IoT devices, and CLI tools where the user authenticates on a separate device.
---@class gcp.ces_v1.LfA2aV1DeviceCodeOAuthFlow
---@field tokenUrl? string Required. The token URL to be used for this flow.
---@field deviceAuthorizationUrl? string Required. The device authorization endpoint URL.
---@field scopes? gcp.ces_v1.StringMap Required. The available scopes for the OAuth2 security scheme.
---@field refreshUrl? string The URL to be used for obtaining refresh tokens.

---Defines a security scheme using HTTP authentication.
---@class gcp.ces_v1.LfA2aV1HTTPAuthSecurityScheme
---@field bearerFormat? string A hint to the client to identify how the bearer token is formatted (e.g., "JWT"). Primarily for documentation purposes.
---@field scheme? string Required. The name of the HTTP Authentication scheme to be used in the Authorization header, as defined in RFC7235 (e.g., "Bearer"). This value should be registered in the IANA Authentication Scheme registry.
---@field description? string An optional description for the security scheme.

---Deprecated: Use Authorization Code + PKCE instead.
