---@field refreshUrl? string The URL to be used for obtaining refresh tokens. This MUST be in the form of a URL. The OAuth2 standard requires the use of TLS.
---@field scopes? gcp.ces_v1.StringMap The available scopes for the OAuth2 security scheme. A map between the scope name and a short description for it. The map MAY be empty.

---`Message` is one unit of communication between client and server. It can be associated with a context and/or a task. For server messages, `context_id` must be provided, and `task_id` only if a task was created. For client messages, both fields are optional, with the caveat that if both are provided, they have to match (the `context_id` has to be the one that is set on the task). If only `task_id` is provided, the server will infer `context_id` from it.
---@class gcp.ces_v1.LfA2aV1Message
---@field messageId? string Required. The unique identifier (e.g. UUID) of the message. This is created by the message creator.
---@field extensions? gcp.ces_v1.StringList The URIs of extensions that are present or contributed to this Message.
---@field referenceTaskIds? gcp.ces_v1.StringList A list of task IDs that this message references for additional context.
---@field contextId? string Optional. The context id of the message. If set, the message will be associated with the given context.
---@field metadata? gcp.ces_v1.DocumentMap Optional. Any metadata to provide along with the message.
---@field parts? gcp.ces_v1.LfA2aV1PartList Required. Parts is the container of the message content.
---@field role? gcp.ces_v1.LfA2aV1MessageRoleEnum|string Required. Identifies the sender of the message.
---@field taskId? string Optional. The task id of the message. If set, the message will be associated with the given task.

---@alias gcp.ces_v1.LfA2aV1MessageList gcp.ces_v1.LfA2aV1Message[]

---@alias gcp.ces_v1.LfA2aV1MessageRoleEnum "ROLE_UNSPECIFIED"|"ROLE_USER"|"ROLE_AGENT"

---Defines a security scheme using mTLS authentication.
---@class gcp.ces_v1.LfA2aV1MutualTlsSecurityScheme
