---This resource represents a long-running operation that is the result of a network API call.
---@class gcp.ces_v1.Operation
---@field done? boolean If the value is `false`, it means the operation is still in progress. If `true`, the operation is completed, and either `error` or `response` is available.
---@field error? gcp.ces_v1.Status The error result of the operation in case of failure or cancellation.
---@field metadata? gcp.ces_v1.DocumentMap Service-specific metadata associated with the operation. It typically contains progress information and common metadata such as create time. Some services might not provide such metadata. Any method that returns a long-running operation should document the metadata type, if any.
---@field name? string The server-assigned name, which is only unique within the same service that originally returns it. If you use the default HTTP mapping, the `name` should be a resource name ending with `operations/{unique_id}`.
---@field response? gcp.ces_v1.DocumentMap The normal, successful response of the operation. If the original method returns no data on success, such as `Delete`, the response is `google.protobuf.Empty`. If the original method is standard `Get`/`Create`/`Update`, the response should be the resource. For other methods, the response should have the type `XxxResponse`, where `Xxx` is the original method name. For example, if the original method name is `TakeSnapshot()`, the inferred response type is `TakeSnapshotResponse`.

---Event sent by the client or background worker to resume an assistant session after an asynchronous Long-Running Operation (LRO) completes.
---@class gcp.ces_v1.OperationCompletedEvent
---@field operationName? string The operation resource name (e.g. `operations/{op}`).
---@field error? gcp.ces_v1.Status Optional canonical error status if the operation failed.
---@field status? string Status of the operation run (e.g. "SUCCEEDED", "FAILED", "CANCELLED").
---@field targetResourceName? string The primary resource targeted or produced by the operation (e.g. evaluation run ID, app ID, dataset ID).
---@field operationType? string The operation type or tool name (e.g. "run_evaluation", "copy_app", "export_app").
---@field metadata? gcp.ces_v1.DocumentMap Optional structured result metadata (e.g. pass_rate, total_examples, export_uri).
---@field deduplicationToken? string Optional deduplication token (e.g. UUID) to prevent duplicate turn execution from concurrent browser tabs.

---@alias gcp.ces_v1.OperationList gcp.ces_v1.Operation[]

---Structured clarification options the assistant asks the user to choose among, transduced server-side out of the model's turn (the option block is stripped from the streamed and persisted text). The console renders a keyboard-navigable option list docked above the composer.
