---@class gcp.ces_v1.SessionConfig
---@field deployment? string Optional. The deployment of the app to use for the session. Format: `projects/{project}/locations/{location}/apps/{app}/deployments/{deployment}`
---@field historicalContexts? gcp.ces_v1.MessageList Optional. The historical context of the session, including user inputs, agent responses, and other messages. Typically, CES agent would manage session automatically so client doesn't need to explicitly populate this field. However, client can optionally override the historical contexts to force the session start from certain state.
---@field useToolFakes? boolean Optional. Whether to use tool fakes for the session. If this field is set, the agent will attempt use tool fakes instead of calling the real tools.
---@field enableTextStreaming? boolean Optional. Whether to stream text output from the model to the client incrementally as it is generated. Defaults to `false`. * When disabled, the model's text output is buffered, and each text output sent to the client is a complete sentence. Clients can render each text output on a new line. * When enabled, each text output may contain only part of a sentence. Clients should concatenate consecutive text outputs to render the complete response. NOTE: This is only supported for text (non-voice) sessions using StreamRunSession or BidiRunSession.
