---@field image? gcp.ces_v1.Image Optional. Image data from the end user.
---@field willContinue? boolean Optional. A flag to indicate if the current message is a fragment of a larger input in the bidi streaming session. When set to `true`, the agent defers processing until it receives a subsequent message where `will_continue` is `false`, or until the system detects an endpoint in the audio input. NOTE: This field does not apply to audio and DTMF inputs, as they are always processed automatically based on the endpointing signal.
---@field variables? gcp.ces_v1.DocumentMap Optional. Contextual variables for the session, keyed by name. Only variables declared in the app will be used by the CES agent. Unrecognized variables will still be sent to the Dialogflow agent as additional session parameters.
---@field blob? gcp.ces_v1.Blob Optional. Blob data from the end user.
---@field audio? string Optional. Audio data from the end user.
---@field recordingControl? gcp.ces_v1.SessionInputRecordingControlEnum|string Optional. Whether the conversation may be recorded and logged from here on. Use this when the app, rather than the agent, decides what may be kept: for example when the end user has to consent to being recorded before anything about the call can be stored. The value stays in effect until the client sends a different one, so it only needs to be sent when the answer changes. Whatever is in effect when a turn completes decides that turn, both whether its audio reaches the recording bucket and whether its transcript reaches conversation history, BigQuery and Cloud Logging. It covers the agent's side of the turn as well as the end user's. Turns that complete before the client first sends this are recorded according to the app's logging settings, as though the field did not exist. If more than one input in the same request sets it, the last one wins.
---@field event? gcp.ces_v1.Event Optional. Event input.
---@field text? string Optional. Text data from the end user.

